{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789224230,"nonce":"7Fw0qW9jsrS6RaA76FLRF0iGYfs=","title":"Scalar replacement for loop-carried objects (mandelbrot allocates a Complex per iteration)","message":"bench/ash/mandelbrot.wren runs at about 9 s against Ash's 0.68 s. The inner loop rebinds `val = Complex.new(...)` every iteration, so each iteration allocates and the getters read fields through the object. Ash's ScalarReplacement turns the object's fields into per-iteration scalars once the constructor inlines. The existing Sra pass does not handle an object that flows around a loop back-edge; extend it to split a non-escaping loop-carried allocation into per-field block parameters when every use is a field read or write on a known class with inline constructor semantics.","files":null}]}